
# Testing the message flow and taking a trace

A step-by-step runbook for triggering a full UE registration + PDU session
in the lab and capturing/reading the packet trace for it. For static
reference (IPs, ports, node list) see `docs/5g-lab-reference.html`; this
document is about *doing* a test run, not looking things up.

All commands assume you're in `lab/` and your shell has working `docker`
access (`docker ps` succeeds without error — see README.md if not).

---

## 1. What you're actually testing

A single UE "attach" exercises almost every interface in the core, in this
order:

| # | Step | Interfaces involved |
|---|------|----------------------|
| 1 | gNB boots, sets up its NGAP/SCTP association to AMF | N2 |
| 2 | UE sends Initial Registration (SUCI) | N1 (inside N2) |
| 3 | AMF asks AUSF to authenticate the UE, AUSF asks UDM for vectors | SBI (Nausf, Nudm) |
| 4 | 5G-AKA challenge/response, Security Mode Command/Complete | N1/N2 |
| 5 | AMF checks subscription data (NSSAI, access/mobility data) with UDM | SBI (Nudm) |
| 6 | Registration Accept / Complete | N1/N2 |
| 7 | UE requests a PDU session; AMF forwards to SMF | SBI (Namf, Nsmf) |
| 8 | SMF fetches session-management subscription data from UDM, policy from PCF | SBI (Nudm, Npcf) |
| 9 | SMF sets up the session on the UPF | N4 (PFCP) |
| 10 | PDU Session Establishment Accept reaches the UE; `uesimtun0` comes up | N1/N2 |
| 11 | Actual user traffic (e.g. a ping) flows UE→gNB→UPF→internet | N3 (GTP-U) + N6 |

Everything before step 7 is **signaling only** (no user IP traffic).
Step 11 is the only step that produces GTP-U payload packets.

