## 3. Trigger a clean attach

The cleanest, most reproducible way to generate a full attach is to restart
the simulated UE and gNB together. This forces a brand-new NGAP association
and a full Initial Registration (not a GUTI-based re-registration, which
skips some of the steps in the table above).

```bash
kubectl -n core delete pod -l 'component in (ue,gnb)'
```

Kubernetes recreates both pods immediately; the new UE starts attaching
within a few seconds on its own (no further action needed — UERANSIM
auto-registers and auto-requests a PDU session on startup).

**If you see NAS/NGAP errors that don't match anything in §5** (e.g. `AMF
can not select an AUSF by NRF`, `UDM discovery failed`, or repeated
`CONGESTION`/`ILLEGAL_UE` rejects): this is almost always NRF's in-memory
registration table being out of sync with one of the NFs (see
README.md → "Issues hit and fixed" for why). Fix: restart every core NF pod
once, then retry this step.
```bash
kubectl -n core delete pod -l 'nf in (amf,ausf,smf,upf,udm,udr,pcf,nssf,webui)'
# wait ~30s for them all to become Ready, then re-run the pod delete above
```

